From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 21:23:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/83] =?UTF-8?q?kernel/net:=20POSIX=20socket=20conformanc?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20=E2=80=94=20fix=20~15=20bugs=20the=20torture=20suite=20foun?=
 =?UTF-8?q?d?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

torture_net.c (the 347-check network-stack suite) flagged a cluster of
substrate-specific defects. Fix the batch; the suite goes from 24
failing checks to 9 (333/342 pass), with the remainder a large-transfer
wedge (under investigation) and AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM (unimplemented).

af_inet.c:
- socket(): validate protocol against type (STREAM->TCP, DGRAM->UDP);
  a bogus protocol is EPROTONOSUPPORT, not silently accepted.
- bind(): reject re-bind (EINVAL) and enforce EADDRINUSE for a port
  another socket already holds, relaxed by SO_REUSEADDR.
- connect(): a connected stream socket returns EISCONN immediately
  instead of wedging on a second handshake; sync the kernel-assigned
  ephemeral local port back to the socket so getsockname()/the peer's
  getpeername() agree.
- shutdown(): ENOTCONN on a never-connected stream socket.
- sendto(): allow a zero-length datagram (was EINVAL).
- recvfrom(): MSG_PEEK returns data without consuming it (new tcp_peek);
  recv() on a listening socket returns ENOTCONN instead of blocking.
- sock_matches_v4/v6(): a SOCK_STREAM socket never matches datagram
  delivery, and an unbound (local_port==0) socket is no longer a
  promiscuous catch-all — that made stray TCP/UDP sockets swallow a
  copy of every datagram.
- afinet_deliver_v4/v6(): take a for_dgram flag so the udp_input path
  delivers to DGRAM sockets and the ip4_input/RAW path delivers to RAW
  sockets — previously every UDP datagram was enqueued twice
  (duplicate/out-of-order receives).
- SO_REUSEADDR get/set plumbing.

tcp.c: tcp_peek / tcp_peek_nb (MSG_PEEK without consuming).

af_unix.c: socket syscalls return EBADF for a closed/garbage fd
(was ENOTSOCK); getsockopt honours SO_REUSEADDR / SO_RCVBUF / SO_SNDBUF
and returns ENOPROTOOPT for an unknown option (was a silent 0);
setsockopt records SO_REUSEADDR.

inet.c / udp.c / inet.h: thread the for_dgram flag through the two
afinet_deliver_v4/v6 call sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
